exactly is an oxygen mask oxygen masks

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.710
are products which come out of the
bottle like a gel but they start

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:47.340
bubbling with oxygen gas after you put
them on your skin for a bit as you wait

00:00:47.340 --> 00:00:51.030
your skin gets covered in tickly bubbles
and you sort of start to look like a

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:57.000
cloud they're pretty darn entertaining
lots of brands have come out with oxygen

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.520
masks there's brands like bliss Peter
Thomas Roth dr. Brandt Oseque

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:12.630
Sephora and philosophy how exactly do
they get the oxygen into the bottle

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.369
these oxygen products work a lot like
soda water gas gets dissolved in the

00:01:17.369 --> 00:01:21.689
water under pressure so for example
carbon dioxide gas is in soda water

00:01:21.689 --> 00:01:26.100
this gas gets released when the pressure
drops so when you open the soda water

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.549
bottle

00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:40.080
unlike carbon dioxide oxygen doesn't
really dissolve that well in water

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:44.890
instead you have solvents in these
products called perfluorocarbons these

00:01:44.890 --> 00:01:48.700
are stable unreactive carbon-based
compounds that have lots of fluorine on

00:01:48.700 --> 00:01:53.080
them compared to water they can dissolve
about 20 times more oxygen and they've

00:01:53.080 --> 00:01:55.539
been investigated for use in artificial
blood

00:01:55.539 --> 00:01:59.200
these perfluorocarbons can be mixed with
the oxygen and then sealed in a

00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:02.979
pressurized bottle so when it comes out
the oxygen will start fizzing out slowly

00:02:02.979 --> 00:02:06.789
like a bubbly soft drink if you have a
thicker product you might not even need

00:02:06.789 --> 00:02:10.539
a pressurized bottle the thickness of
the product can trap the oxygen inside

00:02:10.539 --> 00:02:15.340
the oxygen gas only comes out when you
massage it over your skin it's a little

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.819
bit like pop rocks there are a lot of
different perfluorocarbon products in

00:02:18.819 --> 00:02:22.569
these oxygen masks the most common ones
are probably perfluorodecalin and

00:02:22.569 --> 00:02:26.709
methyl perfluorobutyl ether but pretty
much anything in the ingredients list

00:02:26.709 --> 00:02:30.910
with the word perfluoro in it will be a
perfluorocarbon there are also some

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:35.140
oxygen masks that get oxygen from
hydrogen peroxide composing so for

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:38.650
example philosophy's oxygen peels are
like this you'll want to keep these

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:42.280
products away from dark fabrics because
peroxide will bleach them but the ones

00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:47.109
that have perfluorocarbons will be safe
I'm using this bubble purifying and

00:02:47.109 --> 00:02:51.280
charcoal face sheet mask the key
ingredients in this there are some

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.160
humectants so dipropylene glycol and
glycerin

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.959
there's also methyl perfluorobutyl
ether methyl perfluoroisobutyl ether

00:02:58.959 --> 00:03:04.299
and these two ingredients will dissolve
the oxygen and make it foam up again

00:03:04.299 --> 00:03:07.420
when I put this on there are also some
other cool ingredients in this like

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.760
centella and a bunch of other fruit
